# Layout (ideal-stack hierarchy + Studio grid/flex)

**Owns:** `section → container → content` band model for ideal-stack, and the Studio detail for Law G6 + policy S2 in `natural-document-flow.mdc`. **Laws** (native tags, stamps, no JS layout): `architecture/semantic-html-css.mdc`.

## Golden sentences (ideal-stack)

1. **Compose** `section → container → content` (primitives / composites / buttons).
2. **Section owns the band** — full-bleed background + **side and vertical padding** (gutters).
3. **Container owns width** — parent track / align (prefer grid/`1fr` + padding). Not page gutters, not band color. **Do not** add leaf `max-w-*` / `min-w-0` clamps — `natural-document-flow.mdc` / ADR 0007.
4. **Flex / Grid own layout flow** — row/col/gap/columns + grow (`flex-1` / `1fr`). Not page spacing; not `h-full` by default.
5. **Everything else** = primitives (heading, text, button, …) or composite **slots**.
6. **Painted inset surface** (bg on a box that is not the band) → **border + radius + inset padding**. Never a naked fill.

### Who owns what

| Layer | Owns | Never |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **`section`** | Band `background`, **padding (sides + top/bottom)**, landmark `<section>` | Content max-width; stuffing CTAs as raw HTML without primitives |
| **`container`** | Align + participate in parent width (grid/flex) | Side/page gutters; page-band background; unbordered filled "cards"; new `max-w-*` layout clamps |
| **`flex` / `grid`** | Direction, wrap, gap, columns / tracks / grow | Page band padding; leaf max-width shells; `min-w-0` / casual `h-full` |
| **`card` / inset panel** | Surface fill **with** `border-line` + `rounded-xl` (or `lg`) + inset padding | Bare `bg-paper-raised` with no edge |
| **Composites** (`blog-hero`, …) | Editorial structure + slots (+ layout knobs) | Site chrome `<header>` / `<footer>`; owning page max-width or page gutters |

```html
<section data-as-component="section" …>           <!-- band + gutters -->
  <div data-as-component="container" …>         <!-- width via parent track / align -->
    <section data-as-component="blog-hero" …>   <!-- composite / slots -->
```

### Background taste

| Situation | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| Full-width page band | Set `background` on **`section`** only (`muted` → `bg-sand`, `surface` → `bg-paper-raised`, `brand` → `bg-accent`) |
| Transparent band | `section` `background: transparent` — page `bg-paper` shows through |
| Side / vertical rhythm | **`section` `padding`** (default includes `px-4 md:px-8`) — not Container, not composites |
| Inset panel / "card" look | Raised fill **only if** paired with **`border border-line`**, **`rounded-xl`** (or `lg`), and **padding** |
| Container with fill, no border | **Forbidden** — reads like a broken floating slab |

### Copy alignment

| Mode | Container | Copy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Left stack (default) | `align: left` | left |
| Center stack | `align: center` | center **every** copy block / CTA row |

Never center the width box while leaving title/CTAs left-aligned inside (floating-left-in-a-centered-box).

### Footer & chrome

- Full-width footer **band** = wrapping **`section`** (`background: muted`). Semantic `<footer>` inside = links/chrome only — **no** band fill on the footer tag itself.
- Site top bar stays `<header>` (nav) — never reuse that landmark for `blog-hero`.

### Motion (restrained)

≤1 delight beat per section; ≤2 motion sources per page when adding animation. Prefer `prefers-reduced-motion` respect.

## Shell grid / flex content (Studio chrome)

**Audience:** primarily **Studio chrome** (`apps/studio/**`). Ideal-stack uses the **general** Law G6 in `natural-document-flow.mdc` (2D skeletons OK on marketing/components) — not this shell-first tightening.

**Golden sentence:** In Studio product chrome, **grid is for shell / stage tracks** (and rare true 2D tools). **Content panes use the pane recipe** (`flex-col` + one scroll leaf). Never use content `grid` to "fix" truncation.

| Layer | Tool | Examples |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Shell** | CSS **grid** OK once | `data-shell-body` columns; main `auto`/`1fr` stage |
| **Pane / column** | Law G3 — `flex flex-col overflow-hidden` + `flex-1 overflow-y-auto` | Left AI rail, chat column, settings body, recents rail |
| **Row chrome** | **One** `flex` / `inline-flex` | Session tabs, avatar + bubble turn, toolbar, list row |
| **Copy / MD** | **block** | Bubbles, prose, lists — no grid |
| **2D chrome tools** | Component **grid** OK | Design atlas, true multi-track inspectors — not lists |

```
shell grid (body)
  └─ pane flex-col overflow-hidden
       ├─ header / tabs   shrink-0
       ├─ scroll body     flex-1 overflow-y-auto
       └─ footer          shrink-0
            └─ content: flex peer-row → block prose
```

### Forbidden (Studio G6 + S2 + G10)

| Don't | Why |
| --- | --- |
| `grid` + `grid-rows-[auto_1fr_auto]` inside a grid cell for chat/settings/lists | Nested tracks fight; children expand past the cell |
| Content `grid-cols-1` "to force width / truncate" | Escape hatch — use Law G5 / Studio truncate recipe |
| Grid "for consistency" on every nested host | Flex column fills leftover without a second track graph |
| Content `grid` whose children also `grid` for fill | Overflow / double min-size traps |

### Prefer flex for panes (Law G3)

| Need | Use |
| --- | --- |
| Tabs + filling log + composer | Parent `flex flex-col overflow-hidden`; log `flex-1 overflow-y-auto` |
| Narrow rail list + ellipsis titles | Law G5 / Studio S1 — row `overflow-hidden` + title `truncate` |
| Avatar beside bubble | Turn `flex`; sharing child `flex-1` + overflow |
| Shell body left / main / right | **One** body grid — panes inside are flex |

Shell `overflow-hidden` on the flex column so `flex-1` children can shrink and scroll — prefer overflow, not `min-w-0` / `contain-inline-size` (Studio S1). CQ `@container` on panes remains OK.

## Checklist

- [ ] `section` owns band + gutters; `container` owns width (no leaf `max-w-*` clamps)
- [ ] Bordered inset surfaces have border + radius + padding (no naked fill)
- [ ] Copy alignment matches container mode (no floating-left-in-centered-box)
- [ ] New fill layout in a rail/pane → Law G3 flex recipe, not nested `grid-rows`
- [ ] `grid` only if this node is a **shell/stage** band or a documented **2D chrome tool**
- [ ] Truncate failures → G5 / S1, not content grid
- [ ] Ideal-stack 2D marketing → general G6 in `natural-document-flow.mdc`

